%SIXMD 1
# @?DLINK - LINK DOBJ OBJECTS AND DARC ARCHIVES

## DESCRIPTION

DLINK LINKS DOBJ1 OBJECTS AND DARC1 ARCHIVES INTO A DAIMOS DXR2 EXECUTABLE.
THE NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION IS A MULTI-PASS STREAMING LINKER: OBJECT TEXT, DATA,
AND RELOCATIONS ARE READ FROM FILES AS NEEDED SO LARGE OBJECTS DO NOT REQUIRE
A SECOND IN-MEMORY COPY.

USAGE IS 'DLINK -O OUT.DXR [-M MAP] [-B OCTAL] [--PURE] [--RT-REQUIRED] [--DAIMOS-UUO-RELAX] INPUT ...'.

THE NATIVE LINKER SUPPORTS THE OPTIONS REQUIRED FOR DAIMOS USERLAND
SELF-HOSTING. HOST-ONLY IMAGE-CONSTRUCTION FEATURES SUCH AS FOLD PLANS,
ABSOLUTE IMPORT MAPS, AND MRES PACKAGE GENERATION REMAIN IN THE HOST DLINK.

## @?OPTIONS

### @?-O OUT.DXR
WRITE THE LINKED DXR2 EXECUTABLE.

### @?-M MAP
WRITE THE DEFINED-SYMBOL MAP AS NATIVE S6REC TEXT.

### @?-B OCTAL
LINK THE IMAGE AT THE GIVEN OCTAL BASE ADDRESS.

### @?--PURE
MARK THE IMAGE PURE IF NO DEFINITE TEXT WRITE IS FOUND; FAIL IF SUCH A WRITE
IS PRESENT.

### @?--RT-REQUIRED
MARK THE RESULT AS REQUIRING THE REAL-TIME FACILITY.

### @?--DAIMOS-UUO-RELAX
REPLACE DIRECT CALLS TO ONE-UUO DAIMOS SYSCALL VENEERS WITH THE CORRESPONDING
MONITOR UUO WHEN SAFE.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?INPUT
DOBJ1 OBJECT OR DARC1 ARCHIVE. ARCHIVE MEMBERS ARE LOADED ON DEMAND TO RESOLVE
UNDEFINED GLOBAL SYMBOLS.

## LIMITS

THE NATIVE LINKER USES FIXED METADATA TABLES: 48 OBJECTS, 8 ARCHIVES, 384
GLOBAL DEFINITIONS, AND A 0300000-WORD MAXIMUM STORED IMAGE. BSS MUST FIT THE
DXR 077777-WORD BSS FIELD, AND THE LINK BASE PLUS IMAGE PLUS BSS MUST REMAIN
WITHIN THE 18-BIT ADDRESS SPACE. EXCEEDING A BOUND IS AN ERROR RATHER THAN A
HEAP-GROWTH REQUEST.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - LINK COMPLETED
### @?1 - INVALID INPUT, UNDEFINED SYMBOL, LIMIT, RELOCATION, OR FILE ERROR

